@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 05 - Accept-Language (en, ar) sets the request culture. Problem titles, fixed problem details, and
# FluentValidation messages follow it; Content-Language echoes the resolved culture. Run against a Development
# API (`docker compose up -d` first). Compare with diagnostics.http requests 4, 6, 7 (no Accept-Language: English,
# byte-identical to before this story).

### 1. Arabic validation (acceptance criterion) - 400, title "فشل التحقق من صحة البيانات",
### errors.Name[0] "'Name' لا يجب أن يكون فارغاً.", header Content-Language: ar
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{ "name": "", "lines": [] }

### 2. Same body, English - title "Validation failed", "'Name' must not be empty.", Content-Language: en
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "name": "", "lines": [] }

### 3. Parent-culture fallback - ar-SA,en;q=0.5 negotiates to ar (never ar-SA: no Hijri calendar)
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar-SA,en;q=0.5

{ "name": "", "lines": [] }

### 4. Unsupported culture - fr falls back to the default, English
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: fr

{ "name": "", "lines": [] }

### 5. No Accept-Language header - defaults to English
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "lines": [] }

### 6. Status-code pages path - 404 title "غير موجود" (bare 404, no controller involved)
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Nope
Accept-Language: ar

### 7. Exception-handler path - 500 title "خطأ داخلي", detail "حدث خطأ غير متوقع." (no exception text).
### Fails first if UseCrmRequestLocalization runs after UseExceptionHandler (Probe 1).
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Diagnostics/throw
Accept-Language: ar

### 8. Domain rule - 422 title "مخالفة لقاعدة عمل", detail stays the English domain message, code Sample.DuplicateLine
POST {{host}}/api/Admin/Samples
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: ar

{ "name": "Dup", "lines": ["a", "A"] }
